In article <18804@pasteur.Berkeley.EDU> kemnitz@postgres.UUCP (Greg Kemnitz) writes:
>A Nethack 3.0 Spoiler List:

>...  Polymorphed items will keep their
>states as far as pluses and blessed/cursed states go, except for wands.

No.  Wands keep their charges except for wishing.  Rings and tools with charges
or plusses don't keep them since charges and plusses are not uniformly meaning-
ful among them.

>1:  Dipping in pools will eventually remove the curse from stuff - ...

Fountains, not pools.

>1:  Having a monster steal your cursed items.  Nymphs will steal cursed armor
>	and weapons.  Be sure that you have dropped everything else, however, 
>	before trying this.

Also, a succubus/incubus (depending on gender) will remove your armor...  (If
it is tame or peaceful, you can use #chat to do so anyway.)

>2:  A scroll of destroy armor can be used to destroy cursed armor.  Be sure
>	to take off all your other armor before reading the scroll. *

Exception:  if the scroll and object are both cursed, it won't work and you
will take damage besides.

>3:  If you eat a tin of deep-fried monster meat, your rings, gloves, and
>	weapon will fall on the floor even if these are cursed.

Not if they are cursed (unless you compiled the game without HARD).

>1:  Dig pits around one corner of the shop.  When you are done, the shop
>	should look something like this:
>	|           ^@|
>	+@          ^^| 
>2:  Now dig a pit underneath you - twice.
>The shopkeeper will not step into the pits, so s/he can't grab at your pack.

False.  Under some circumstances (however it's not reliable since the code
was written improperly) he'll jump over the pits and get you anyway.  To rob
the shop, dig like this:
        -----------
        |         +^  <-- you fall in this
        +@        |
        |         |
        -----------

Do not carry any unpaid stuff when doing this.  Digging the hole in the wall is
possible since the wall "seems" too hard to dig into but is not.  Now dig the
trapdoor; you'll fall.  Come up again, pick up all the items, and now you can
fall in the trapdoor again and steal.

>1.  Wand of wishing (can't be wished for).

Yes it can, it just won't have any charges!

>5.  You'll need one musical instrument.

No you won't.  You can levitate over the water (or polymorph into something
which flies, such as a vampire lord) and then go all around the moat to the
other side, where there's a door.

>o  Throwing gems at unicorns gives you luck - as does sacrificing at altars.

Not quite: throwing a known valuable gem at a unicorn of the wrong alignment
gives you a random luck change, either up or down.
